cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If BayesBreak is useful to your research, please cite both the software
  and the companion paper using the entries below.
title: "BayesBreak: Generalized Hierarchical Bayesian Segmentation"
abstract: >-
  BayesBreak is a Python library for offline Bayesian segmentation of
  univariate and multivariate sequences. It supports irregular designs,
  multi-sequence shared-boundary pooling, grouped and latent-group
  templates, exact conjugate inference, and explicitly approximate
  nonconjugate block calculations with certified perturbation bounds.
